WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.101
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:05.905
I am here in studio with
Michael Che and Colin Jost!

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.507
Um, so --

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.242
I say we're back!
We're here with Col--

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.078
We'll get you --
-I thought we were

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.413
going to switch seats
during the commercial.

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:16.683
-I thought it wouldn't be good.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.385
-[ Laughter ]
-He made the decision.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.354
-Hey, you know.
-A lot of things have happened

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.922
since -- First of all,
thanks again for coming in.

00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:25.991
Colin, really, thank you.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:29.028
But since you guys have helped
me out with the shows

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.530
in quarantine
and you Zoomed in --

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.165
And I appreciate you doing that.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.567
Since you've been on, Colin,
your book went to

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.702
"The New York Times"
Best Seller list, dude.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.372
Congrats.
-Thank you.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.741
Dude, he is a "New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:44.944
Don't you ever forget it.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.946
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.382
-Big deal.
-How's the house?

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.216
'Cause we were talking about
you bought a house last time.

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:53.153
-Yeah. I did buy a house.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.887
-Ah-ha!
-Okay. Okay.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.724
It's not a competition.
I mean...

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.525
-I haven't moved in yet
because apparently

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.361
it takes a long time to close.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.329
I didn't know this.
-No, you can't just buy it?

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.532
-Usually, where I go to live,
it's an apartment,

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:10.202
and you give the money,
and then they give you a key.

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.304
End of transaction.

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.640
Now, like, with a house,
you have to, like, wait.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.909
They have to make sure
that everything's up to code.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.479
I don't know about any codes.
I've got to get a lawyer.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:23.283
They got to take down a shed.
It's annoying. It's a mess.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.750
-The shed wasn't up to code?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.886
-The shed wasn't up to code.
They took it down.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.788
I'm just going to put it back up
as soon as they leave.

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:32.992
-I cannot believe
that there is a code for sheds.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.194
-There's a code for sheds.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.861
-I've never seen a shed
and thought,

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.163
"That looks up to code."
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:39.998
-"That's a good shed."
-"That shed looks up to code."

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:42.601
-It's an outside closet, man.
Give the shed a break.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:46.071
-I'm so happy that Chris
is there. Chris Rock hosting.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:47.907
Do you have Chris Rock stories?

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.610
-I remember being backstage
at the -- at the --

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.645
When they did the benefit
after Hurricane Sandy,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.814
they did it at
Madison Square Garden.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:58.117
And I was there
with Bobby Moynihan.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.787
We were going to do a bit
where he was Drunk Uncle.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.655
And so we were
waiting backstage.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.757
And it's all huge
musical acts, right, there.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.826
The Who, Rolling Stones, all...

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.328
And we're waiting to go on,
you know,

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.629
and Chris Rock wanders over,
and he's like,

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.332
"Hey, guys, how's it going?"
We're like, "Oh, good."

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.568
He goes, "So, The Who's on now,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.237
and then Rolling Stones
are going to go on,

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:19.805
and then between that,

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.275
they're going to
send you guys out there...

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.910
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.979
...to do a comedy bit.
Is that what's happening?"

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:30.649
And suddenly,
we're like, "Yeah.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:32.118
Yeah, that's what's happening."

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.520
He was like, "Hey.
Best of luck."

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.890
He goes, "I'll tell you
something. I'll be watching."

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.459
-"Yeah, I'm definitely
not going out there."

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.028
-My story's not as good.

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.064
-No!
-Your story's great.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:48.501
-Okay, it's a silly story, but
one time I was doing "Top Five."

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.336
He had a movie "Top Five."
-Loved that.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.938
-And I got to meet
Rosario Dawson

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.874
for the first time,
and I was smitten.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.375
-Yeah.
-And I remember

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.511
her talking to me.
She was so nice to me.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.346
And she was like,
"You look so familiar.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.814
Do I know you from somewhere?"

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.383
And I was like,
"I don't think so."

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.585
And she was like, "Are you sure?
Have we never met?"

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253
And I was like,
"I don't think we've ever met."

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.156
And I just hear Chris Rock on
the other side of the hall go,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:14.260
"You're not sure if you've
met Rosario Dawson or not?!"

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.695
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.630
And I was like,
"I know I've never met her."

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.233
"You're not su--
Have you met Beyoncé?!"

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:23.435
No, I've never met Beyoncé.
-[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:26.739
"How do you not know
if you've met Rosario Dawson?!"

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.707
I don't know.
-He is unbelievable.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.743
I love him so much.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.414
And then Jim Carrey
is going to, maybe?

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.749
-Yeah. Yeah.
You talked to him personally.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.751
-It seems like it's possible.
There was a debate.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.953
And it seems like people
were talking about the debate.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.622
-Yeah, there was a debate.
Oh, my God.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:45.091
-Seems like it got
pretty good reviews.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.692
-Colin, it did not
get good reviews at all.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.828
-I haven't read all the reviews
yet, but some of the ones...

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.097
-Jim Carrey playing Joe Biden.
-Yes.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.231
-That would be amazing.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.533
Maya Rudolph
doing Kamala Harris.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.203
It's all a possibility?
You don't want to say anything.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.938
You can't spoil it.
-Never know.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.674
-That wouldn't be fun.
-We can't spoil who wins.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.743
We can't -- We can't spoil it.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.944
-You can't --

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.580
-Could be Jim Carrey.
Could be Sinbad.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.184
-Sinbad.
Sinbad's not playing Joe Biden.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.519
-I don't know!
I've heard things.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.488
-"I heard some things."
-People are talkin'.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.357
-It's going to be awesome.
It is Saturday night.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:20.659
It is live. It is on NBC.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.628
Best of luck. Break a leg.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.029
I know you guys are brilliant,

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:25.498
and you've got to go up
and write some funny stuff.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.800
So thanks so much for
taking time, coming here.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.002
And thanks for being live
on behalf of everyone,

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:31.470
doing that for us.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.107
Michael Che, Colin Jost.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:37.443
"Saturday Night Live" returns
this Saturday. That's right.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.079
On NBC with host Chris Rock
and musical guest

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.081
Megan Thee Stallion.
We'll be right back.

